               <head>Tarjumah-'i Ṣavā'iq al-muḥriqah by Muḥammad Bābā Kalān al-Muftī</head>
               <msContents
                  class="http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2009127610 http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85121390">
                  <summary>An abbreviated translation of <persName xml:lang="ar-Latn-x-lc"
                        key="person_100387532">Ibn Ḥajar</persName>’s anti-Shiʻah polemic <title
                        xml:lang="ar-Latn-x-lc" key="work_600">al-Ṣawāʻiq al-muḥriqah</title>,
                     completed in 979/1571 by Muḥammad Bābā known as Kalān al-Muftī of Samarqand. </summary>
                  <msItem xml:id="Uk_Delhi_Persian_264-item1">
                     <author key="">
                        <persName xml:lang="fa-Latn-x-lc">Muḥammad Bābā Kalān al-Muftī</persName>
                        <persName xml:lang="fa">محمد بابا کلان المفتی</persName>
                     </author>
                     <title xml:lang="fa-Latn-x-lc" key="">Tarjumah-'i Ṣavā'iq al-muḥriqah</title>
                     <title xml:lang="fa">ترجمۀ صواعق المحرقه</title>
                     <incipit xml:lang="fa">حبیب حضرت آله طبیب علت کناه محمد رسول الله صلی الله علیه
                        و علی آله و سلم بقرب و مجد [؟] خود الخ </incipit>
                     <explicit xml:lang="fa">و بعضی اورا از خلفأ راشدین عد کرده بودند شمهٔ از اوصاف
                        او ذکر کرده ختم کتاب بران کرده شد </explicit>
                     <colophon>(<locus>f. 127r</locus>) Completed 10 Rajab 979 (28 November 1571) in
                           <origPlace>Samarqand</origPlace>. This however most probably reflects the
                        date and place of completion of the work rather than the date of copying
                        which appears to be late 18th or early 19th century. </colophon>
                     <note>
                        <p>Lacks folio 1. </p>
                     </note>
                     <note>
                        <p>The work comprises an introduction and eight chapters which are described
                           in the preface. Chapters one and two of the original work are here
                           omitted. </p>
                     </note>
                     <note>
                        <p>Title supplied. </p>
                     </note>
                     <textLang mainLang="fa" otherLangs="ar">Persian and Arabic</textLang>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
